  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Deloitte Consulting has $2B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, across 534 awards and an average award size of $3.7M. Obligations are down 32.9% year over year. Deloitte Consulting’s obligations peaked at $3.3B in FY24 and then moved to $3B in FY25 before falling to $2B in FY26. The General Services Administration is the largest buyer, obligating $571M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $311M and the Department of Defense with $304M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market for Deloitte Consulting, with $937M obligated, and Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services is the second-largest market with $430M. Other notable markets include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences with $248M and Engineering Services with $196M. The data reflect partial current-year totals and award counts for the fiscal year to date, showing concentrated demand in IT and management consulting along with significant work from civilian agencies and the Department of Defense.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Deloitte Consulting’s federal business trended recently?",
        "body": "Obligations rose from $2.4B in FY21 to $3.3B in FY24, then declined to $3B in FY25 and to $2B in FY26. Obligations are down 32.9% year over year. The FY2026 to date total covers 534 awards with an average award size of $3.7M. This shows a recent pullback from the FY24 peak into the current fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Deloitte Consulting’s biggest federal customers and markets?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration leads buying with $571M, followed by Department of Veterans Affairs at $311M and Department of Defense at $304M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market at $937M, with Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services next at $430M. Health, research, and engineering markets also appear among the top categories."
      }
    ]
  },
